# B0: the BUILD-ONLY job of the window, run BEFORE A0 while production still serves. C2_ACTIONS=build opens no card, resets nothing and stops nothing: it makes the
# one image of the window (the thin tt-vllm layer over the P8 base, with the three lever modules and their kernels) from the pushed tp4/samp-draft commit.
# THE TAG MUST BE FRESH. The build step skips a tag that already exists on the host, so a reused tag would silently serve an old image: the driver checks tp4-samp-1 is
# absent from the host's images before it pushes this job, and a later commit needs a new tag in every template.
# Pass: the build log ends with the image tagged, the closure and provenance checks of the build pass. Stop rule: any failure stops the window before production is touched.
# Duration (estimate): 18 min typical, 90 at worst (the first build after a base change).
# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the four-card tp4/samp-draft window (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over
# .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/samp-draft and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN. Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a
# registry: the cards are resolved at run time. The window's jobs are templates only: no tag is pushed from this branch by its author.
# ONE IMAGE FOR THE WHOLE WINDOW: C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-samp-1 is the image B0 builds from the pushed tp4/samp-draft commit while production serves (it carries
# tp4_shard_argmax, tp4_draft_conv and tp4_draft_heads and their kernels, which are new); a later commit needs a new tag in every template.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=build
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-samp-1
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4
